<p>The United States and Iran exchanged fire on Thursday around the Strait of Hormuz during a month-old ceasefire that began on April 8. U.S. Central Command said Iranian forces launched missiles, drones and small boats at the destroyers USS Truxtun, USS Rafael Peralta and USS Mason as they transited the waterway; it said U.S. forces intercepted the threats and struck Iranian military facilities responsible for the attack. Iran&#x27;s Khatam al-Anbiya Central Headquarters said the United States violated the ceasefire first by targeting an Iranian oil tanker and another vessel near the strait and by attacking areas in Hormozgan province, including Bandar Khamir, Sirik and Qeshm Island. Iranian officials said their forces responded by attacking U.S. military vessels east of the waterway and south of Chabahar port. In a Truth Social post, President Trump said the transit was successful; he later said the ceasefire remained in effect and described the exchange as a &quot;love tap&quot; or &quot;trifle,&quot; while warning Iran to sign a deal quickly.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/etBUb24AhU2TbxfYddVHy-HyYj4mRCLqGWKiDYs3X9UI7NYS1hPur8x334mC2Xd6vstoHOHQgvYO1iq0Bl0W56XIYbuqgPvRdwbCkoFa0dfRs6DmowHtQJOzeKbUjs6Y9ZgZUzu3WP4zSoMeNkPVHLB4DEEWBd0uVzMCviBKxok2Auux2wyd-ZTRJEW1KtbZmFXwXKFUYVabVtNHWiFUkRwQ-9qEx6JwP2SjNDy37X3R2MeApSnFCOhzW6pBY2N--_4' alt='USS Rafael Peralta near a vessel that U.S. Central Command said was attempting to sail to an Iranian port while the U.S. enforced its blockade, released April 24, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Targets reported: Reports citing U.S. officials said U.S. strikes hit Iranian sites at Qeshm port and Bandar Abbas near the strait.</li><li>Transit route: CENTCOM said the ships were transiting the Strait of Hormuz into the Gulf of Oman when the attacks occurred.</li><li>War losses disputed: A U.S. admiral said U.S. forces sank six small Iranian ships, while Iran denied any had been sunk.</li><li>Nuclear talks: The exchange occurred while Washington was awaiting Tehran&#x27;s response to a U.S. proposal that would stop the fighting but leave issues including Iran&#x27;s nuclear program unresolved for now.</li><li>Escort operation: Military Times reported that Project Freedom, the U.S. escort operation for ships moving through the strait, has since been paused.</li></ul><blockquote>Three World Class American Destroyers just transited, very successfully, out of the Strait of Hormuz, under fire. There was no damage done to the three Destroyers, but great damage done to the Iranian attackers - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Central Command: CENTCOM described the response as self-defense and said it did not seek escalation, while remaining positioned to protect U.S. forces. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/05/07/g-s1-120978/u-s-military-intercepted-iran-attacks-navy-ships-hormuz'>NPR</a>)</li><li>Iranian state media: Citing an unnamed military official, state media claimed U.S. naval units were forced to retreat after sustaining damage from Iranian missile strikes, a claim that conflicted with U.S. statements that the destroyers were undamaged. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/us-navy-came-under-missile-fire-after-us-attack-iranian-oil-tanker-iran-state'>Al-Monitor</a>, <a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/trump-says-great-damage-done-iranian-attackers-after-us-navy-destroyers-came'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump said Washington was still negotiating with Iran and suggested a deal could be reached soon as tensions continued in the Strait of Hormuz. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/videos/trump-says-iran-talks-advancing-despite-rising-tensions-at-hormuz/article70953926.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>United Arab Emirates: Abu Dhabi denied Iranian media claims blaming the UAE for the attacks, Ynet reported. (<a href='https://www.ynetnews.com/article/hytsq00qcbg'>Ynet</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3>